{"seq":4,"id":"NT1","type":"note","at":"2026-11-13T13:16:55Z","by":"AC1","prev":"sha256:3063421a11d8e94f109188ba920f7bd0a542358a42d0ffc7907898fdf10f8fcc","content_hash":"sha256:e3d1761ed13d84db90b05e221fb770babf2e766ba8f847830d5dbb5b96b7c8d6","supersedes":null,"origin":null,"body":{"text":"Brief requirements (from the supervisor, 2026-11-13): (1) a claimset based on prediction.md of entrylib/study-planning (v0.2, commit 104ba1c); (2) a pure literature summary: each claim is a statement of good practice supported by the paper(s) it rests on, no new computation; (3) one claim per default and one per Avoid item (supervisor's choice); (4) what not to do is stated as separate claims, with references; (5) papers cited by DOI, captured from open-access copies where they can be reached (supervisor's choice); (6) kept in the lab, on branch claimset/prediction-good-practice of entrylib/study-planning."}}
{"seq":5,"id":"Q1","type":"question","at":"2026-11-13T13:18:41Z","by":"AC1","prev":"sha256:d1f7e271848c571780e43b439b775fff43639bf528482f4b0b206523e2215c9e","content_hash":"sha256:ea166ff5a1277b6093bbfbdf25921abd55f620a75f80cfda96d2c898ad1f1e14","supersedes":null,"origin":null,"body":{"text":"Which measures and tests should a study use to evaluate and compare predictions (point forecasts of a mean, a median or a quantile, prediction intervals, predictive distributions, class probabilities), according to the methodological literature on evaluating forecasts and classifiers?"}}
{"seq":6,"id":"TM1","type":"term","at":"2026-11-13T13:18:43Z","by":"AC1","prev":"sha256:bd34c7ccf4b97dddeaba992085a327d35fe1f9bc47d7143aad0e4439119ea36d","content_hash":"sha256:230927a8121c7bdcf0b6cd3a5c337a62e0d90eb0a813cb7733fa8d79ca969c7b","supersedes":null,"origin":null,"body":{"term":"consistent scoring function","kind":"concept","definition":"A scoring function (an error measure for point forecasts) is consistent for a functional of the predictive distribution, such as the mean, the median or a quantile, when its expected value is lowest when the point forecast equals that functional.","source":"doi:10.1198/jasa.2011.r10138"}}
{"seq":7,"id":"TM2","type":"term","at":"2026-11-13T13:18:45Z","by":"AC1","prev":"sha256:d1a6633f5832875f1e2d9fa3f8c0ea185b4f6b236572b19a520da8eea7df3051","content_hash":"sha256:ed2d78936a4aaf3b7e5cb5bae3197af1396295eed5766fbd5093370a2d0e1d21","supersedes":null,"origin":null,"body":{"term":"proper scoring rule","kind":"concept","definition":"A scoring rule for probabilistic forecasts is proper when its expected value is best when the forecast distribution equals the distribution of the outcome, and strictly proper when it is best only then.","source":"doi:10.1198/016214506000001437"}}
{"seq":8,"id":"TM3","type":"term","at":"2026-11-13T13:18:47Z","by":"AC1","prev":"sha256:3cfd5c3efefa56913d884bebb8a9dc0d5de7e9e05fc82ff09e602a9196ed216e","content_hash":"sha256:38bb5eebbed7113c190c70d54cba7b9a5e6ee825e4696a29a87c857c8178a8c5","supersedes":null,"origin":null,"body":{"term":"point forecast of the mean","kind":"concept","definition":"A single-valued forecast meant to equal the mean (expected value) of the outcome's distribution given the information available.","source":"doi:10.1198/jasa.2011.r10138"}}
{"seq":9,"id":"TM4","type":"term","at":"2026-11-13T13:18:49Z","by":"AC1","prev":"sha256:af1aa684be39740178f8b613a6a54cc8408617a523174c25defaa7d3d52ff9c7","content_hash":"sha256:392554bbb6a4d92cae8ab378207412110a8880e090660c6f73c425cff0d5bf31","supersedes":null,"origin":null,"body":{"term":"point forecast of the median","kind":"concept","definition":"A single-valued forecast meant to equal the median of the outcome's distribution given the information available.","source":"doi:10.1198/jasa.2011.r10138"}}
{"seq":10,"id":"TM5","type":"term","at":"2026-11-13T13:18:50Z","by":"AC1","prev":"sha256:7bba665ff7eed64bfb38c326dcfec73d15fef364f068389e678f070bbe9e62be","content_hash":"sha256:97fdef7ac1f2f4328b71fe50ceba1fce8e9593d95081401ce63c99761ad6b594","supersedes":null,"origin":null,"body":{"term":"RMSE","kind":"variable","definition":"Root mean squared error: the square root of the mean of the squared differences between outcomes and point forecasts.","source":"doi:10.1016/j.ijforecast.2006.03.001"}}
{"seq":11,"id":"TM6","type":"term","at":"2026-11-13T13:18:52Z","by":"AC1","prev":"sha256:d084ff6ebecc231db97c2d71f27c6e52030b9aa17e27016dc7538f8fed73687d","content_hash":"sha256:7817dd3f16d40daec98cf41c6b3c5bdb69711a932659e798fa6db02d651e5e0d","supersedes":null,"origin":null,"body":{"term":"RMSSE","kind":"variable","definition":"Root mean squared scaled error: the RMSE of a series' forecasts divided by the in-sample RMSE of the one-step naive forecast of that series, so that series on different scales can be averaged.","source":"doi:10.1016/j.ijforecast.2021.11.013"}}
{"seq":12,"id":"TM7","type":"term","at":"2026-11-13T13:18:54Z","by":"AC1","prev":"sha256:0e3d0b1b58536bd6f58f626a66a24f3135cfaacfbfe4105d2bf939bb142a47f5","content_hash":"sha256:ed9b6d080b203e659d8c5fb35d71366c94bdbd5572b299d742cada3a5fc4fd4e","supersedes":null,"origin":null,"body":{"term":"MAE","kind":"variable","definition":"Mean absolute error: the mean of the absolute differences between outcomes and point forecasts.","source":"doi:10.1016/j.ijforecast.2006.03.001"}}
{"seq":13,"id":"TM8","type":"term","at":"2026-11-13T13:18:56Z","by":"AC1","prev":"sha256:70d1b9f797214c07b02db1a619d38ff6f8d7f865995d717ed51d99289b1cec35","content_hash":"sha256:65cfb702f93120a76bc70cc51a0ff0c27ccc01a6f0cdc546b3065a101f06b096","supersedes":null,"origin":null,"body":{"term":"MASE","kind":"variable","definition":"Mean absolute scaled error: the MAE of a series' forecasts divided by the in-sample MAE of the one-step naive forecast of that series.","source":"doi:10.1016/j.ijforecast.2006.03.001"}}
{"seq":14,"id":"TM9","type":"term","at":"2026-11-13T13:18:57Z","by":"AC1","prev":"sha256:234d868996ec0058d376e9ed522ca2614e3939f15ad7fe6f20e9f9996d89c0f6","content_hash":"sha256:abb938d63e53460f0cc39c58005c18944f2be49381b5389f68fb4c45ae526241","supersedes":null,"origin":null,"body":{"term":"MAPE","kind":"variable","definition":"Mean absolute percentage error: the mean of the absolute differences between outcomes and point forecasts, each divided by the outcome.","source":"doi:10.1016/j.ijforecast.2006.03.001"}}
{"seq":15,"id":"TM10","type":"term","at":"2026-11-13T13:18:59Z","by":"AC1","prev":"sha256:9e0da15b97eca886853b6500766c89d757ef1dbaf766766fc8bd6734f107fa03","content_hash":"sha256:0c1a6fd540d013a7dda2ca5269c58e577473b74c7664591894957f290f534dfd","supersedes":null,"origin":null,"body":{"term":"sMAPE","kind":"variable","definition":"Symmetric mean absolute percentage error: the mean of the absolute differences between outcomes and point forecasts, each divided by the mean of the absolute outcome and the absolute forecast.","source":"doi:10.1016/S0169-2070(99)00007-2"}}
{"seq":16,"id":"TM11","type":"term","at":"2026-11-13T13:19:01Z","by":"AC1","prev":"sha256:9823d2de43e5747827057e21efd12150d5b425c9c7f13bb77b6aeb74eb46fd2e","content_hash":"sha256:7efeb7f48fd843111e14761e41e240cb1c1dcdda8f1672dbadb3350516e57c86","supersedes":null,"origin":null,"body":{"term":"median of order -1","kind":"concept","definition":"The beta-median with beta = -1: the point forecast that minimises the expected absolute percentage error; for positive outcomes it lies below the median.","source":"doi:10.1198/jasa.2011.r10138"}}
{"seq":17,"id":"TM12","type":"term","at":"2026-11-13T13:19:02Z","by":"AC1","prev":"sha256:30e45c72fc5170a7c5e59cff0df15a0c2dfd5ce4c8adda5f855d8a4ba62abe9e","content_hash":"sha256:dacbe3aa9b2a429807be18e7d94d50c26c2358a695a486c50d4f9d80b7ee523e","supersedes":null,"origin":null,"body":{"term":"pinball loss","kind":"variable","definition":"The quantile (asymmetric piecewise linear) loss at level tau: tau times the error when the outcome is above the forecast, and (1 - tau) times the absolute error when it is below.","source":"doi:10.1198/jasa.2011.r10138"}}
{"seq":18,"id":"TM13","type":"term","at":"2026-11-13T13:19:04Z","by":"AC1","prev":"sha256:2fed9aeac59464c1201ad9f2a182af9fcbc4c46a64b5c208be32e4a41402e3e7","content_hash":"sha256:337e025ca59365516625ce462664c2e22eabf6e36fb1f4fadcc5f38dbaa9905a","supersedes":null,"origin":null,"body":{"term":"interval score","kind":"variable","definition":"The score of a central (1 - alpha) prediction interval: its width plus 2/alpha times the distance by which the outcome falls outside it.","source":"doi:10.1198/016214506000001437"}}
{"seq":19,"id":"TM14","type":"term","at":"2026-11-13T13:19:06Z","by":"AC1","prev":"sha256:77e01b322925d6d0f2b813698e596f9c14e0aa43b587492352171ab8cafc88b4","content_hash":"sha256:f88776818c5718488cbed9874171f2ab6fa82f58474905b54a8d5303435d6820","supersedes":null,"origin":null,"body":{"term":"coverage","kind":"variable","definition":"The share of outcomes that fall inside the prediction intervals, compared with their nominal level.","source":"doi:10.1198/016214506000001437"}}
{"seq":20,"id":"TM15","type":"term","at":"2026-11-13T13:19:08Z","by":"AC1","prev":"sha256:167b2074f6df3c4777d7fad35e2993e632a431f184828bb6cc6457168f7f3680","content_hash":"sha256:f8f02f152d0c6774ff19846d2431f53bd906536a017915ca4cc4555225e8d693","supersedes":null,"origin":null,"body":{"term":"CRPS","kind":"variable","definition":"Continuous ranked probability score: the integral over thresholds of the squared difference between the forecast's cumulative distribution function and the step function at the outcome.","source":"doi:10.1198/016214506000001437"}}
{"seq":21,"id":"TM16","type":"term","at":"2026-11-13T13:19:09Z","by":"AC1","prev":"sha256:fd2587137dfc56d73ac057ddd3cdf99d385bb6e1900195895b78f7b69138da1b","content_hash":"sha256:0ad39d85644508992a1d215b18ecff40a36239fc8d3f5550e141328ec284ce6d","supersedes":null,"origin":null,"body":{"term":"log score","kind":"variable","definition":"The logarithmic score: the negative logarithm of the forecast density (or probability) at the outcome.","source":"doi:10.1198/016214506000001437"}}
